[{"code":"top_level_list_changed","severity":"error","span":{"file":"Main.beni","start":{"line":26,"col":8},"end":{"line":26,"col":19}},"title":"TOP-LEVEL LIST CHANGED","message":"`update` changes `model.todos` in place, but when the program starts it is\n`Seeds.seed`, a top-level value.\n\n26|main = Tea.sandbox { init = λ⊤ → { todos = Seeds.seed }, update = update, view = view }\n          ^^^^^^^^^^^ the runtime hands `update` the model here\n\n`Seeds.seed` is defined in Seeds.beni:\n\n3|seed = [ \"milk\", \"eggs\" ]\n  ^^^^ the top-level list is defined here\n\nA top-level value is shared by every part of the program and never changes:\nchanged in place, it would change for every part that reads it.\n\nBuild the value inside `init ⊤`, so that each call makes fresh lists:\n\n    init ⊤ = …\n\nCall that function where the model is made. Wrapping `Seeds.seed` in\n`λ⊤ → Seeds.seed` still returns the same shared value.\n\nThis is the language's rule for top-level values, whether or not anything else\nreads the list. `init` builds its model; a top-level value it returns is still\nshared (ownership-checker.md §22.2)."}]
